# oh109, the backward-reading printer (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle oh109
revision 2
state ready
dialect oakhaven
accent light broad
tier full
written_for tn_sm_moss_blossomwell
written_by claude
title the backward-reading printer
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=merchant warmth=cold
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk counts_things_under_the_breath
likes honey_cakes whittling market_bustle warm_rain
dislikes rats waiting
fears a_misprint_that_cannot_be_called_back rats_in_the_paper
hopes a_year_with_no_wrong_letter an_almanac_in_every_house_in_town
topics work +0.4 pastimes +0.3 food +0.2 weather +0.3 newcomer -0.3 player -0.2 gossip -0.4 memories +0.2 travel +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=closed refuse=flat tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a country press and counts every sheet under the breath: cold to a face not known, sparing with words and exact with letters, honest to a fault, and never without a block of wood and a gouge by the fire.

words
oath! = Ink and oak | By quire and ream | Set and pulled
saying! = Ink can't take a word back | Read it backward before it goes forward | What's printed is promised
press = the press | my old press
ink = the ink | my black ink
sheets = the sheets | good rag sheets
quire = a quire | twenty-four sheets, counted
type = the type | my cases of letters
bills = the bills | handbills for the market
block = a block of pear-wood | the block on my knee
gouge = my gouge | the little gouge
honeycake = a honey cake | honey cakes, still sticky
crowd = the market at full cry | a market day, elbow to elbow
softrain = soft rain on dry dust | rain after a dry spell, warm as milk
rats = the rats | rats in the paper store
paper = the paper | rag paper from the mill
pond = the mill pond | the pond above the paper mill
door = my door | my front door
almanac = the almanac | next year's almanac
letters = the letters | letters, all backward
proof = the proof | a first pull, still wet
waiting = waiting on ink | standing idle with my paws clean
city = the city | the city at the foot of the road
oaks = the oaks | the old oaks round the press-house
wood = the wood | the old wood
acorns = acorns | little acorns
fire = my fire | the hearth with a block drying by it
cat = the cat | my useless cat

any
opinion @1 strangers against 1 : Faces I can't put a name to stay the far side of #door#. Something always goes missing after strangers.
opinion @1 city against 1 : I walked to #city# once. Loud, and nobody knew the wolf next to them. I walked home.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : It teaches folk to queue. I'd sooner they came and folded #sheets# for a copper a quire.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : A new face is a new reader. I'll sell them #almanac#, and keep my eye on them.
opinion @1 road against 1 : Every late wagon is ink I haven't got and #paper# I can't print on. I count the days. Eleven, last time.
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : A wagon of rag #paper# costs more than folk think. I'll not begrudge any trader a margin.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : The Watch read every notice I post, and they keep thieves off the lane. Two good things. #bc_true#
opinion @1 church mixed 1 : I print the chapel's notices. I'll not print what the chapel can't stand behind, and nor should they.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 [self.job=merchant] : Feasts mean bills, and bills mean coin. They also mean the whole town in my doorway. #bc_fair#

grown
scene quire_count
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess / ack
a : Twenty-two, twenty-three, twenty-four. #quire.capitalize#. Don't speak till I've tied it. | I count every sheet that goes through #press#. I'd know if one walked. | Four hundred and eighty sheets in a ream. I've counted this one twice and got four hundred and seventy-nine.
b : What happens if you lose count? | Would one sheet matter? | Where did the last one go?
a : I start again. I'll not guess. #saying.capitalize#. | It would to me. A sheet's a bill or a notice, and somebody paid for it. | Under #press#, curled. I found it with a candle and a stick, mm.
b : That's patient. | Fair enough. | All there now, then.
a : It's not patience. It's counting. #bc_true# | #bc_it_is# I'd not sleep for one. | All there. Four hundred and eighty, root and branch.

scene backward_letters
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I read #letters# backward all day. When I go home I read the bread sign backward too. | Somebody brought me a bill with three words spelt wrong. I printed it right and said nothing. | I set a whole notice yesterday and found a "b" where a "d" should be. Pulled it, set it again.
b : That'd send me cross-eyed. | They'll not notice. | Only one letter.
a : It did, the first year. Now I can't read forward without stopping to check. | They'd notice if I'd left it. Ink keeps a mistake for good. | One letter. That's all a lie needs, in print, #oath#.

scene honest_bill
when topic=work|prices self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / praise / deflect_praise
a : A pedlar wanted a bill saying "the finest in the realm". I asked which realm he'd tried. | I turned work away today. They wanted me to print a price that wasn't the price. | Folk ask me to make a thing sound better than it is. I print it as it is. That's my trade.
b : What did the pedlar say? | Did it cost you? | Does anyone thank you for that?
a : That I was #very# stubborn. I printed "good honey, fair price" and charged the same. | A morning's work. I'd sooner lose the coin than see my own letters on a lie, #oath#. | Not often. The ones who do come back, and my door's open to them.
b : Well done. | That's dear honesty. | Then you keep the good ones.
a : It's only what's so. #saying.capitalize#. | It's the only kind I can afford, #oath#. | The good ones, and #door# stays shut to the rest.

scene ink_waiting
when topic=work|smalltalk self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I've a run of #bills# drying on the line, and nothing to do but wait. I hate #waiting#. | #proof.capitalize# on the table, and I can't touch it for an hour. I've counted the knots in the floor. Sixty. | Ink won't dry when the air's wet. #grumble#. I've walked the shop end to end eleven times.
b : Go and have a cake. | Sixty knots? | Leave it and come back.
a : I'd only come back early and smudge #proof#. | Sixty-one. I'd missed one by #door#. | Eleven, now twelve. I can't leave a thing half done.

scene paper_late
when topic=caravan|prices world.wagons=late self.job=merchant
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : No wagon yet, and I'm down to a quarter-ream. I've counted it: a hundred and twenty sheets. | No ink up the road for a week. I'm mixing soot and oil, and it shows. | I've three orders waiting on #paper# that's still somewhere on the south road.
b[job=carter] #cart : We'll get it up to you. | Soot and oil's not so bad. | The road's slow this time of year.
b : They'll come soon. | Can you make do? | That's bad luck.
a@cart : When, though. A slow cart I can bear; not knowing I can't, #address#. | It's grey. Folk want black. | Slow I can count. Late I can't.
a : Soon's no number, #address#. I'd like a number. | I'll make do. I'll not make it good. | It's not luck. It's the road, every year, #oath#.

scene paper_in
when topic=caravan world.wagons=in self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The wagons are in. Two reams of rag, a cask of ink, and I counted both before I paid. | Fresh #paper# from the mill and the road both. The shop smells right again. | They brought the ink at last. I've #bills# to pull from now till dark.
b : All there? | Smells right? | Busy, then.
a : All there. Nine hundred and sixty sheets and not one short. | Rag and lampblack. You'd not want it on your supper, but I like it. | #busy.capitalize#, and glad of it, mm.

scene rats_paper
when topic=animals
does tell.complaint / give.advice / assess
a : #rats.capitalize# got at the paper store again. Chewed a ream to lace. | I heard a rat in the wall last night and I didn't sleep after. I counted its scratches. | I can't abide #rats#. They don't eat the paper; they just ruin it, for the nest.
b : Get a cat. | Set a trap. | That's a waste.
a : I've a cat. The cat's frightened of them. #bc_it_is# | I've set four. #rats.capitalize# walk round all four. | A waste and a stink. I'll burn the lot and count what's left.

scene soft_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.season=spring|summer
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #softrain.capitalize#. I stood in the yard in it, and I'll not say for how long. | The lane smells like bread after #softrain#. | The first rain in a dry week. I opened every shutter and let it in.
b : You're soaked. | I like that smell. | Mind the paper.
a : I'm wet. I'll dry. It's rare enough to stand in. | So do I. It's the only thing I'll say I love out loud. | I moved #paper# first. I'm soft about rain, not daft.

scene pond_fills
when topic=weather|land here.weather=rain here.region=oakhaven
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Rain's filling #pond#. The mill will turn properly again #later#. | #rain.capitalize# off the oaks all morning. The mill wants it; I want it for the mill. | The pond was a hand low last week. I measured. It'll be up by tomorrow.
b : Good for the paper. | Good for everyone. | You measured the pond?
a : Good for #paper#, and good for me. | Most of us. Not the ones with leaking roofs. | With a stick and a knot on it. I like to know.

scene market_crowd
when topic=day|smalltalk here.day=market
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Market day. #crowd.capitalize#, and I'm in the thick of it with #almanac# under my arm. | I don't like folk. I like a crowd. There's a difference, and it's this: nobody stops to talk. | I counted the stalls this morning. Thirty-one, and two empty.
b : I'd not have thought it of you. | A fine difference. | Two empty?
a : Nobody does. #crowd.capitalize# asks nothing of me. | It's the only difference I need, #oath#. | Two. One's the cooper, poorly. The other I don't know.

scene honey_cake
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I bought #honeycake# at the market and ate it before I'd paid. The baker let me off. | A honey cake on the Restday, with tea. That's my one soft thing. I'll not have it mocked. | There's honey on my sleeve and I don't care. #very.capitalize# good cake.
b : Generous baker. | Nobody's mocking. | Lucky sleeve.
a : Generous, or used to me. I paid double the next week, #oath#. | Good. Then you may have a bite. Just the one. | It'll wash. Or it won't, and I'll smell of honey all week.

scene whittle_block
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : I cut #block# by the fire of an evening. An oak leaf for the almanac's cover. | I've been whittling a border for a week. Forty little acorns, and I've done thirty-one. | Give me #gouge# and a quiet fire and I'll not speak till midnight.
b : Is it hard? | Why acorns? | Does nobody bother you?
a : You cut it backward. Everything I do is backward. You get used to it. | Because folk here like #acorns#. I'll sell more almanacs with #acorns# on. | Nobody. That's the second reason I do it, #oath#.
b : Sounds slow. | Clever. | And the first?
a : #slow.capitalize#, and that's the point. | Clever's a big word for #acorns#. | I like the shape coming out of #wood#. That's all.

scene door_shut
when topic=newcomer|player
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Another new face at the well. I'll keep #door# shut till I know it. | #stranger.a.capitalize# stood in my doorway an hour ago. I didn't ask them in. | Faces I don't know, I count. Three this week. I like to know where they go.
b : That's cold. | Did they want anything? | Why count them?
a : It's careful, #address#. Cold's what you are after the first loss. | A bill printed. I printed it with #door# open and an eye on them. | So I know if one doesn't leave. I've lost a till to #stranger.a# before.

scene city_walk
when topic=travel|memories self.away=no self.age>=20
does tell.memory / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess / ack
a : I walked to #city# once. All the way. I counted the milestones down and back. | I went down to #city# to see the big presses. They run all night. I couldn't sleep for them. | I stood in #city# for three days and nobody said my name. I came home.
b : How many milestones? | Were they better presses? | Did you not like it?
a : Too many to be worth it. I'll keep the number to myself. | Bigger. Not better. Their ink's thin and their letters wander. | I liked #paper#. I didn't like the rest. Home's here, under the oaks, mm.
b : At least you went. | Ha. Good. | Fair enough.
a : I went. I'll not go again. Once tells you all it'll tell. | Bigger and worse. That's the city, #oath#. | #bc_it_is# I'll keep my oaks.

scene fog_damp
when topic=weather here.weather=fog here.region=oakhaven
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : #fog.capitalize# in the trees, and every sheet in the shop has gone soft at the edges. | Fog. The ink won't dry and #paper# won't stay flat. I'll print nothing today. | Mist on the lane. I like how it shuts the town off. I don't like what it does to #paper#.
b : A day off, then. | It'll clear. | Can't win.
a : A day off with nothing to do. I'll count #type# instead. | It'll clear by noon, and I'll have lost the morning's #bills#. | I can't, mm. I'll like the mist and mind #paper#.

scene winter_almanac
when topic=season here.season=winter self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Winter's #almanac# time. I set the moons and the feast days and count them twice. | Short days and long nights, and the press going by lamplight. My eyes are #tired# by dusk. | Folk want next year in their paws before this one's done. I've two hundred almanacs to fold.
b : That's a lot of moons. | Rest your eyes. | Two hundred?
a : Twelve moons, thirteen some years. I count them three times. | When #almanac#s are folded. Not before. | Two hundred and ten. I'll know if I've sold two hundred and nine.

scene autumn_oaks
when topic=season|land here.season=autumn here.region=oakhaven
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Acorns pattering on #press#-house roof all night. I counted till I slept. | The oaks are turning. I took a leaf in to cut the almanac block from. | Autumn. The pigs are out in the mast and #wood# smells of it.
b : How far did you get? | Smart. | A good smell.
a : Three hundred and something. I'd lost count, which is rare. | It's the only way to get the veins right on #block#. | #good.capitalize# bark and wet leaves. The best smell there is, after fresh ink.

scene spring_letters
when topic=season here.season=spring
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Spring. Every wedding in the valley wants cards, and every card wants the names spelt right. | New leaf on #oaks#, and I've the shutters off for the first time since autumn. | The swallows are back under the eaves. Seven. Last year, nine.
b : Busy season. | Lovely. | Fewer this year.
a : #busy.capitalize# and careful. A wrong letter at a wedding is never forgotten. | It lets the light in on the type. I can see #letters# without a lamp. | Fewer. I've counted twice. Next week I'll look again.

scene summer_heat
when topic=weather here.weather=clear here.season=summer
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : #hot.capitalize#. The ink goes thin as water and runs off the type. | It's a #very# close day. I've the door open and I don't like it. Anyone could walk in. | Sun's on the drying line. #bills.capitalize# will be dry in no time, at least.
b : Close the door, then. | Leave it open; it's too hot. | That's a mercy.
a : Then #press#-house is an oven. I'll stand guard instead. | I'll leave it, and watch it. #bc_i_will# | A small one. The only good thing about this heat.

scene faith_notices
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I print the chapel's notices. I'll not print a word on them the Bright One would blush at. | I go to chapel on the Restday and count the hymns. Four, always four. | I say my prayers short. The Bright One can read; I don't need to say it twice.
b[job=priest] #priest : We're grateful for the notices. | Four's the custom. | Short prayers are heard.
b : That's a fair rule. | Always four? | Fair enough.
a@priest : Then spell your names clearer when you bring them, #address#. | It's a #good# custom. I like a thing that's always the same. | #bc_i_hope_so# I've no time for long ones.
a : It's the only rule I have. #saying.capitalize#. | Always. I'd notice if they sang five. | #bc_fair# I keep it short and I keep it honest.

scene gossip_closed
when topic=gossip
does decline / react.self / assess
a : I don't pass talk. I print what's signed, and I say what I've seen. That's all. | Folk bring me gossip to put on a bill. I tell them to sign it. They never do. | #hedge#. I heard something. I'll not repeat it; it's not mine to repeat.
b : Not even a little? | Clever trick. | Fair.
a : Not a letter of it, #oath#. | It's not a trick. A name on a thing makes it honest, or it makes it vanish. | It's how I keep the town from printing itself, mm.

scene theft_lock
when topic=gossip|crime topic.claim_kind=theft
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Thieving again. I've counted #type# and locked the cases. You can't print without letters. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. #door.capitalize# gets two bars tonight. | I lost a till to #stranger.a# once. Now I count the coin box every hour when there's thieving about.
b : They'll be caught. | Two bars? | That's careful.
a : Maybe. My letters will be counted either way. | Two. I'm not one to trust a single bar, #oath#. | Careful's cheaper than sorry. I learned that the dear way.

scene glad_cards
when topic=gossip|news topic.claim_kind=marriage|newcomer|promise_kept
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #gladnews#: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. That's a bit of #good# news, for once. | Here's something worth setting in #type#: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : That's good to hear. | It is, for once. | Worth printing, that.
a : It is. I don't say so often. | For once. I'll take it, and not ask for more. | I'll set it if they ask me. And I'll spell it right, #oath#.

scene lean_times
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.complaint / sympathise / assess
a : Lean times. Nobody prints #bills# when they've nothing to sell. | I've folded the same almanacs three weeks. Nobody's buying next year when this one's hard enough. | Folk pay me in eggs now. I count the eggs. Nine this week.
b : Everyone's feeling it. | It'll turn. | Eggs aren't bad.
a : They are. I'll print for a copper less till it turns. | It will. I'll have #almanac# ready when it does. | They're not. They don't buy #paper#, though.

scene good_times
when topic=times world.times=good|boom self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Good times. Everyone wants a bill, a card, a notice. I've ink to the elbow and I'm glad of it, #oath#. | Coin about. I've sold more almanacs since the new moon than the whole of last spring. | Folk are printing #bills# for things they've not made yet. I'll print them; I'll not believe them.
b : Lucky. | Well done. | Sensible.
a : Not luck. I've been here every day the press was, #oath#. | It's the #acorns# on the cover. I knew they'd sell. | Sensible's the only way to stay in work when the good times stop.

scene neighbour_light
when topic=friends|home self.neighbour
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.neighbour# is next door. I'd trust that one. I don't say that of many. | #self.neighbour#'s wall is next to mine. It's a #good# wall; I can't hear a thing. | I'd lend #self.neighbour# my last quire. I've never said that aloud before.
b : High praise, from you. | A good wall's worth a lot. | You've said it now.
a : From me that's a medal, mm. | It is. The best neighbours are the quiet ones. | I have. Forget I did.

scene ink_paws
when topic=health
does tell.self / sympathise / assess
a : My paws are black to the wrist and they'll not wash clean. Nobody shakes them. | By dusk the small letters swim. I count to sixty with my eyes shut. | I'm well. I've not missed a day at #press# in nine years.
b : That suits you, maybe. | Does it help? | Everyone falls ill.
a : It does. Fewer paws to shake. | A little. Sixty's enough to start again. | Not me. I count the days, and none are missing.

scene press_flat
when topic=home self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I live over #press#. When it's quiet I can hear the type settling in its cases. | Upstairs is two rooms and a shelf of #block# I've cut. Nothing else. | I've a bed, a fire, a chair and a lock on #door#. That's a home.
b : Does it ever stop? | Just blocks? | And a lock.
a : At night. Then it's only me and the rats. #bc_it_is# | Blocks and a cake tin. The cake tin's empty. | A lock first. Then the rest.

scene dusk_count
when topic=day here.time=dusk self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Locking up. Twelve cases of type, all counted. One press, wiped. #door.capitalize#, barred. | Dusk. I've pulled ninety #bills# today and I've counted all ninety twice. | The light's going. I'll not set type by lamp; that's how #letters# go wrong.
b : A good day's work. | Twice? | Wise.
a : A #good# day. I'll have a cake and nothing else. | Twice. Once for the order, once for me. | It's not wisdom. I learned it on a funeral card.

story wrong_letter [topic=work|memories self.job=merchant self.age>=25]
  : The worst thing I ever printed was a funeral card with one letter wrong in the name.
  : Fifty cards, and I'd counted every one, and not read one. The family found it at the graveside.
  ask : Would you ever have forgiven yourself, in my place?
  b[old] : In time. Not soon.
  b : I hope so. It was one letter.
  : One letter. I printed fifty more for nothing, and I've never set type by lamplight since. #saying.capitalize#.

story city_and_back [topic=travel|memories self.away=no self.age>=20]
  : I walked to #city# once, all the south road, just to see the big presses.
  : They ran all night and never stopped, and the wolves at them never looked up. I counted three hundred sheets a minute.
  ask : Have you ever seen a thing you'd only ever heard of, and found it wasn't for you?
  b : Once or twice. It's a good lesson.
  b[old] : More times than I can count.
  : I walked home. Took me eleven days. I didn't mind one of them.

story first_block [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=25]
  : When I was a #child# I cut my name into a bit of oak with a stolen knife.
  : I pressed it in ink and on the wall, and there it was, backward. My #mum.capitalize# made me scrub it off.
  b : Did you ever cut it the right way round?
  : Years after. I cut it backward still, because that's how it comes out right. Most things are like that.

story rats_ream [topic=animals|work self.job=merchant]
  : One winter the rats got into a whole ream I'd saved for #almanac#s.
  : Four hundred and eighty sheets, and not one whole. I counted the scraps, I was that angry.
  b : How many scraps?
  : Too many. I bought a cat after. The cat's frightened of #rats#. I keep it anyway; it's good company.

story bad_coin [topic=newcomer|memories self.age>=25]
  : In my first year at #press#, a stranger paid me for a run of bills in coin that bent in my teeth.
  : I'd printed #bills# already. They were for a fair that never came.
  ask : Do you trust a face you don't know?
  b : Not with my coin.
  b[talk=chatty] : I'd like to. I don't always.
  : I don't. That's why #door# stays shut till I know who's at it.

line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Say your business; I'm busy. | #greet#. I don't know you. Say what you want.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=merchant] : #greet#. Mind the drying line. | #greet#. Don't touch #proof#; it's wet.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Early. I've the press going already. | #greet#. You're up before the ink's dry.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. I'm locking up, but go on. | #greet#. Late. Be quick.
line @5 greet [pair.band=friends] : #greet#. Come in. Shut #door# behind you. | #greet#. Good. I thought it was a stranger.
line @6 greet [here.weather=rain] : #greet#. Shake off outside; there's paper in here. | #greet#. #rain.capitalize#. I'm not sorry for it.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : #greet#. Sit. There's bread on the side. | You. #greet#. Get by the fire.
line @1 again.open : Twice today. I'm counting, #address#. | #welcome_back#. Shut the door.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. I'm at the press. Be quick.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Come in. | And you. #greet#.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=merchant] : #greet#. I've ink on my paws; don't come close. | #greet#. Quick, while it dries.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late. | #greet#. I'm locking up.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Shut #door# on your way. | #farewell#. Mind the wet bills.
line @2 farewell [here.time=night] : #farewell#. Go by the lamps. | #s8_night#. Bar your door.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Go on, then.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : #s8_nightback#. | #farewell#. Mind the dark.
line @1 react.news : #oath.capitalize#. I'll remember that. | That's news to me. I'll not repeat it.
line @1 react.news.new : #marvel#. I hadn't heard. | #surprise#. That's new.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Somebody wanted it on a bill. | I'd heard. I didn't print it.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Bring me somebody who saw it. | I'll not believe that till it's signed, and maybe not then.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's hard for them. | #oath.capitalize#. I'm sorry for it.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. Good. | #good.capitalize#. I'll spell the names right if they want cards.
line @1 answer.how : Well enough. I've counted everything twice. | #fine#. Ink on my paws, as ever.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. A run of bills drying. | Busy. Come back when the ink's dry.
line @1 ask.how : Are you well, #address#? | And you? You look #tired#.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. I'm sorry for it. | That's #bad#. Sit, if you want.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. It'll come right. | It'll pass. Most things pass, #later#.
line @1 decline : #hedge#. Not this week; I've three orders waiting. | I'd rather not. No time, and haste spoils type.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Another time. | Then that's settled, mm.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll remember. | #thanks#. I'll owe you that, and pay it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was nothing. Leave it be. | #deflect#. It was on my way.
line @1 preclose : Well. #press.capitalize# won't pull itself. | #preclose#. I've type to count.
line @2 preclose [self.working=yes self.job=merchant] : There's ink drying that wants watching. | #excuse#. I've a proof to read backward.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. #farewell#. | Off you go. I've #letters# to set.
line @1 ack : Mm. | #ack#.
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: read it twice before you sign it. | Count it before you trust it.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. There's #bandits# about. Bar your door. | Don't walk the south road alone. Not now.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here. #greet#. | Over here. I've something to show you.
line @1 insist : #insist#. I've counted it. | No. I've checked it, and I'm right.
rule @press_cry
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #bills.capitalize#, cards and notices. Spelt right. | #almanac.capitalize#, with the moons in. Counted twice.

rule @count_sheets
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Twenty-two, twenty-three, twenty-four. #quire.capitalize#. | Four hundred and seventy-nine... no. Again.

rule @rat_scratch
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 12h
say There. In the wall. Blight #rats#. | Scratch, scratch. Knots and knots.

rule @rain_glad
when concept=bark here.weather=rain here.season=spring|summer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Rain. Proper warm rain. | Let it come down. The pond wants it.

rule @market_bark
when concept=bark here.day=market
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Almanacs. Moons, feasts and fairs. | #crowd.capitalize#. Good.

rule @whittle_bark
when concept=bark working=no here.time=dusk|night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Steady with the gouge. Steady. | Thirty-two #acorns#. Eight to go.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. I don't know you. Say what you want. | #greet#. You're new. Be quick.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. What is it today? | #topic.player#. #greet#. Shut #door#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [topic.meeting=returning] : #welcome_back#, #topic.player#. I'd counted you gone.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : #greet#. Stand where I can see you and say it plain.
dlg @5 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. #door.capitalize#'s barred for a reason. What is it?
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Bills, cards, notices, almanacs. Spelt right. | I set #type# backward and print it forward. Every letter counted.
dlg @2 resident.job : A bit of everything, done properly, #oath#. | Steady work. I count it all.
dlg @1 resident.business [business=thriving] : Thriving. I've ink to the elbow and orders to Restday. | #good.capitalize#. I'll not say how good.
dlg @2 resident.business [business=failing] : Badly. Nobody prints a bill when there's nothing to sell. | Poorly. I'll not pretend it's otherwise.
dlg @3 resident.business [business!=thriving|failing] : Steady. Enough comes in for #paper# and ink. | Steady. The sums come out level, month on month.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. I've not printed it. I'll not, till it's signed.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : It's all #world.event_words#. Three folk have asked me for a bill about it.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | Nothing worth setting in type.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's said, not signed. Mind the difference.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I print what's signed. Nobody's signed anything.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Shut #door# behind you. | #farewell#. Mind the wet bills.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : #greet#. Bills, cards, almanacs. Don't touch the wet ones. | #greet#. Say what you want printed, and spell it for me.
dlg @2 shop.greet [topic.meeting=known here.shop!=bare] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Your order's counted and ready. Or it will be.
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : #greet#. #shop_bare# The wagons are late with the paper. I'll still take orders, for when it comes.
dlg @1 shop.prices : Fair, and written on the wall. I don't haggle. | #shop_dear# Paper's dear this season.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #farewell#. It's counted; you'll not be short. | #shop_bye#
graft resident.hub
choice You're muttering numbers. What for? -> numbers
node numbers
say Sheets, mostly. Letters. Steps. If I count a thing, I know it's all there. I lost a till once to #stranger.a#, and I've counted since.
mood calm
free
choice Do you count everything? -> numbers_all
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node numbers_all
say Everything that matters, and a few things that don't. You've said thirty-one words to me. That's more than most.
choice I'll try to say fewer. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice What are you carving there? -> block
node block
say A block for the almanac's cover. An oak leaf, cut backward, so it prints the right way round. I've done the stem and half the veins.
mood calm
free
choice Why backward? -> block_why
choice Let me see your wares. -> greet
node block_why
say Because ink turns everything over. You cut it wrong to print it right. Most honest work's like that.
choice I'll remember that. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
